course: dictionary
lesson: 797
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. «Beer» is one of them. For adults, beer is an alcoholic drink made from grain, usually barley, and hops. Children must never buy or drink it.
explain: Context clues help you choose. «Many grown-ups drink things that change how they feel... alcohol, in wine, beer and spirits, relaxes them» shows that beer is an alcoholic drink for grown-ups. The word also appears in «root beer» and «ginger beer», which have no alcohol and are fine for children to drink.
explain: When you meet a word with more than one meaning, try each meaning in the sentence instead of the word. The meaning that still makes sense is the one the writer means.
fact: Beer is an alcoholic drink for adults, made from grain, usually barley, and hops.
fact: The law says children must not buy or drink beer.
fact: Drinks like «root beer» and «ginger beer» have no alcohol, so children can drink them.
fact: A «beer garden» is an outdoor area at a pub.
fact: Some words, like «beer», have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant.
exercise: «Many grown-ups drink things that change how they feel.» Which of these drinks does the text name as alcohol? | Tea and coffee | Milk and orange juice | *Wine, beer and spirits
exercise: «Most Egyptians were farmers who drank thick beer.» What is beer? | A type of fish | A board game like senet | A kind of bread | *An alcoholic drink made from grain
exercise: Mia says ginger beer and root beer are drinks. Can a child drink them? | *Yes, they have no alcohol | No, they are for grown-ups only | Only at a pub | Only on special days
test: «The beer garden was full on a sunny afternoon.» What is a beer garden? | A fast-food restaurant | A vegetable patch | *An outdoor area at a pub | A type of grain
test: Why must children not drink beer? | Because it is a sort of bread | Because it is too sweet to taste nice | *Because it is alcohol, and the law says children must not drink it | Because it is only sold in winter
exam: Which sentence uses «beer» to mean an alcoholic drink? | Sam drank a bottle of root beer after football | Lily had a glass of ginger beer at the party | Mia shared a can of root beer with her friends | *Dad ordered a beer at the pub
